\pard\s0\li360\sa80\f1\fs19 src/utils/debounce.ts\tab Debounce helper used by search\par
\pard\s0\li360\sa80\f1\fs19 src/theme/ and src/**/theme/\tab Shared colors and screen/component styling\par
\pard\s1\sa220 Data, State, and Persistence\par
\pard\s2\sa120 Product model\par
\pard\s0\sa100 Product records contain id, name, price, category, image URL, and description. A cart item extends a product with an integer quantity. The current catalogue is compiled into the application from src/data/products.ts; editing that file is the direct way to add, remove, or change sample products.\par
\pard\s2\sa120 Cart behavior\par
\pard\s0\sa100 CartProvider exposes cart, addToCart, increment, decrement, total, and itemCount through useCart. Adding an existing product increases its quantity. Decrementing updates quantity and removes entries that reach zero. The total is calculated as the sum of price multiplied by quantity; no tax, discount, or shipping amount is added.\par
\pard\s2\sa120 Local storage\par
\pard\s0\sa100 The storage key is @product_catalog_cart. The provider loads JSON from AsyncStorage at startup and saves cart changes after loading completes. Storage is local to the app installation and is not encrypted or synchronized to another device. A storage read/write failure is logged; the app does not currently present a dedicated recovery message.\par
\pard\s2\sa120 Navigation and search\par
\pard\s0\sa100 The root native stack contains MainTabs and ProductDetails. The bottom tab navigator contains Home and Cart. Product details receive a productId route parameter. Home filtering checks whether the lowercased product name includes the trimmed lowercased query. A pull-to-refresh on Home clears the query; it does not contact a server.\par
\pard\s1\sa220 Installation and Run Instructions\par
\pard\s2\sa120 Prerequisites\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa90 \bullet\tab Node.js 22.11.0 or later (as declared by package.json).\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa90 \bullet\tab npm, included with Node.js.\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa90 \bullet\tab Android: Android Studio, Android SDK, a configured emulator or USB device, and a compatible JDK. Follow the React Native environment setup guide for version-specific requirements.\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa90 \bullet\tab iOS: macOS with Xcode, Ruby/Bundler, and CocoaPods. iOS builds cannot be run natively from Windows.\par
\pard\s2\sa120 Install dependencies\par
\pard\s0\sa100 From the repository root, run:\par
\pard\li360\sa120\f1\fs19 npm install\par
\pard\s2\sa120 Start Metro\par
\pard\s0\sa100 In one terminal, start the JavaScript bundler:\par
\pard\li360\sa120\f1\fs19 npm start\par
\pard\s2\sa120 Run on Android\par
\pard\s0\sa100 With an emulator running or an Android device connected, open a second terminal at the repository root and run:\par
\pard\li360\sa120\f1\fs19 npm run android\par
\pard\s2\sa120 Run on iOS\par
\pard\s0\sa100 On macOS, install CocoaPods dependencies when first setting up or after native dependency changes, then run the iOS app:\par
\pard\li360\sa80\f1\fs19 bundle install\par
\pard\li360\sa80\f1\fs19 bundle exec pod install\par
\pard\li360\sa120\f1\fs19 npm run ios\par
\pard\s0\sa120 Keep Metro running while the native app starts. Native build tools and simulator/device configuration must be installed separately.\par
\pard\s1\sa220 Testing and Verification\par
\pard\s2\sa120 Automated commands\par
\pard\s0\sa100 Run the Jest test suite:\par
\pard\li360\sa100\f1\fs19 npm test -- --runInBand\par
\pard\s0\sa100 Run ESLint:\par
\pard\li360\sa100\f1\fs19 npm run lint\par
\pard\s0\sa120 The current App.test.tsx test is a smoke test that verifies the root app renders. It does not cover cart calculations, persistence, search filtering, navigation behavior, or native device builds.\par
\pard\s2\sa120 Manual acceptance checklist\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa80 \bullet\tab Home renders eight products with names, categories, and prices.\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa80 \bullet\tab Search matches product names without case sensitivity; clearing via pull-to-refresh restores the full list.\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa80 \bullet\tab Opening a product shows the selected product's data.\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa80 \bullet\tab Add, increment, and decrement update cart quantity, badge, line totals, and overall total.\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa80 \bullet\tab Removing the final unit displays the empty-cart state.\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa80 \bullet\tab Cart contents reload after closing and reopening the app.\par
\pard\s1\sa220 Limitations and Troubleshooting\par
\pard\s2\sa120 Known limitations\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa90 \bullet\tab Product images require internet access and are supplied by picsum.photos; image availability and exact imagery are not controlled by the app.\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa90 \bullet\tab The displayed product rating is a fixed 4.5, not catalogue data or a review average.\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa90 \bullet\tab FREE delivery is presentation only; there is no shipping calculation or checkout flow.\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa90 \bullet\tab Search is limited to product names. Catalogue, prices, and descriptions are static.\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa90 \bullet\tab The cart is device-local. There are no user accounts, cross-device sync, or backend backup.\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa90 \bullet\tab The empty-cart refresh handler does not fetch or modify data.\par
\pard\s2\sa120 Common setup issues\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa90 \bullet\tab Metro connection or bundle errors: confirm npm start is running from the repository root, then reload the app.\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa90 \bullet\tab Android build/device not found: confirm Android SDK environment setup, start an emulator or connect an authorized device, and check the React Native environment doctor output.\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa90 \bullet\tab iOS command unavailable: iOS native builds require macOS and Xcode; use an Android target on Windows.\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa90 \bullet\tab Images absent: check device internet access; remote image URLs are used by the sample catalogue.\par
\pard\s0\li360\fi-180\sa90 \bullet\tab Cart appears empty after reinstall or app-data clearing: local storage is tied to the installation and is not backed up by a service.\par
